Aqualicia is listed as hydrolysed vegetable&nbsp;
protein in the ingredients list it's actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:22.480
an acacia seed extract mixed with maltodextrin&nbsp;
and this works on aquaporins you might have heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.600
skincare companies talking about nobel prize&nbsp;
winning science and basically what this is is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:33.280
the nobel prize in chemistry in 2003 was given to&nbsp;
two scientists that worked on discovering channels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.640
in cell membranes the cell membrane is like the&nbsp;
outside of a cell the barrier it's sort of like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:43.840
the skin of a cell if we zoom in it looks like&nbsp;
this so for a substance to get into a cell it can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.600
either diffuse through the cell membrane which&nbsp;
is quite tricky some molecules can do it some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.480
molecules can't and you can't really do much to&nbsp;
help that the other option is if it fits into one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.600
of these special channels it has a much easier&nbsp;
time going in it's sort of like a vip entrance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.840
there are tons of different channels and one&nbsp;
type is for water and these are called aquaporins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.560
because they're sort of like a special pore for&nbsp;
water now the top layer of your skin the stratum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:13.040
corneum or what we usually call the barrier this&nbsp;
acts a lot like a cell membrane much like a cell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:18.080
membrane there are aquaporin channels in it and it&nbsp;
turns out a lot of ingredients that interact with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:23.520
these aquaporins are really effective at hydrating&nbsp;
deep in your skin for example one of my favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:28.480
ingredients glycerin my precious is one of the&nbsp;
few molecules that some of these channels let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:33.760
through along with water and it's probably one of&nbsp;
the reasons why glycerin is just so darn good at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.400
a hydrating skin it also turns out that tons of&nbsp;
ingredients that we already use in our skincare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:43.200
products seem to do stuff with aquaporins and some&nbsp;
of them aren't really well known for moisturising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:48.560
so for example caffeine and retinoids are really&nbsp;
good at acting on aquaporins and we all know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:53.360
retinoids do not hydrate your skin so i don't&nbsp;
